      "reasoning": "Age at enrollment is a pre-index patient characteristic. Age can influence the clinical decision to initiate a biologic through age-related comorbidity, safety considerations, eligibility, disease-management preferences, and access. It can also influence whether a patient has initiated biologic treatment by 180 days through those same age-related determinants of treatment uptake and continuation. Thus, the faithful pre-treatment graph treats age as a common cause of index biologic initiation and the 180-day biologic-initiation outcome. The treatment-effect edge is included as required."
